#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# div

#% text
# `div(v, [x1, ..., xn])` gives the divergence `d(v1, x1) + ... + d(vn, xn)` of the vector field `v`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The variables are Cartesian coordinates; `v` has one component per variable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
div([x, y, z], [x, y, z])
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
div([x^2, x*y], [x, y])
#% output
#= 3*x

#% cell
div([-y, x], [x, y])
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The divergence of a curl is zero:

#% cell
div(curl([x*y, y*z, z*x], [x, y, z]), [x, y, z])
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `grad`, `curl`, `laplacian`
